        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rousillon Rupes, Titania\n- People: William Shakespeare, Bertram count of Rousillon\n- Works: All's Well That Ends Well, First Folio, Measure for Measure, Troilus and Cressida\n- Spacecraft: Voyager 2\n- Concepts: Shakespearean problem plays\n\nFacts:\n- All's Well That Ends Well is a play by William Shakespeare that is believed to have been written between 1604 and 1605.\n- All's Well That Ends Well was originally published in the First Folio in 1623.\n- In Shakespeare studies, the Shakespearean problem plays are three plays by William Shakespeare from the late 1590s to the first years of the seventeenth century: All's Well That Ends Well, Measure for Measure, and Troilus and Cressida.\n- Rousillon Rupes is a scarp on the surface of Titania.\n- Rousillon Rupes was named after Bertram, count of Rousillon, in William Shakespeare's All's Well That Ends Well.\n- Voyager 2 first imaged Rousillon Rupes in January 1986.",
